# Citation metadata — read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by
# Zenodo when a release is archived. Version and release date are
# deliberately omitted: the version comes from the git tag
# (setuptools-scm) and Zenodo stamps both from the GitHub release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Electric Tail-Sitter UAV (EDF) – Conceptual Design Study"
abstract: >-
  First-principles conceptual sizing study for a small electric tail-sitter
  VTOL UAV with a single ducted fan and jet-vane control. A Python physics
  package, Jupyter notebooks, CadQuery CAD and OpenFOAM CFD case setups form
  a one-way design pipeline (mission sizing and mass closure, wing and airfoil
  selection, jet-vane and aileron control sizing, vibration isolation,
  fuselage layout, thermal design, solid model, mass properties, electrical
  design and COTS component selection), all validated in continuous
  integration.
authors:
